  "solution": {
    "text": "limit $=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{1+\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{n}}{1-\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{n}}=1,$\r\n\r\nbecause $0<\\frac{b}{a}<1$ implies\r\n\r\n$\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{n} \\rightarrow 0$ as $n \\rightarrow \\infty$"
